KNOWNBUG
capture_this.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ second specialization: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ first specialization: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^Invariant check failed$
--
As test.desc, with a lambda capturing `this' in a virtual member function
of a class template: formatting_scanner<long>::format_arg uses the closure
of formatting_scanner<char>, whose captured pointer has the other type, and
symex stops with an invariant violation (equal_exprt operand types, bin53
too).  Found by reducing libstdc++'s <format> with cvise in 41 lines.
g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG
assertion.
